  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_EDIT
    replacement_chunks {
      target_content: "# MVP Scope vs Future Scope\n\n### 31.1 MVP Scope (SIH 2026 PS 26106 Target)\n- **Core Triage Inbox:** Virtualized table, multi-parameter filtering, quick-peek slideout drawer.\n- **Case Workspace HUD:** Real-time Verdict, Risk gauge, Confidence meter, and Envelope metadata.\n- **RFC 5322 Header Forensics:** Complete Received hop visualizer, transit latency delta calculator, and SPF/DKIM/DMARC matrix.\n- **URL & Domain Analysis:** Defanged link viewer, unshortened redirect chain flow, and homoglyph punycode detection.\n- **Infrastructure & Geolocation:** Origin IP ASN/ISP details and interactive dark-canvas world map route.\n- **Attachment Forensics:** Static metadata, double-extension warning, Shannon entropy gauge, and file hash copying.\n- **Evidence Explorer:** Filterable repository of all `EVD-***` items with one-click deep inspector drawer.\n- **Dedicated Forensic Report View:** In-app report review with explicit visual isolation between System Findings and AI Explanations.\n- **Evidentiary AI Assistant:** Side-dock copilot strictly grounded in Evidence IDs with prompt starters.\n- **First-Class INCONCLUSIVE State:** Dedicated UI for low-confidence or degraded signal cases.\n- **Sober Cybersecurity Design System:** WCAG AA compliant dark palette, zero neon gradients, full keyboard navigation.\n\n### 31.2 Future Scope (Post-Hackathon Enterprise Roadmap)\n- **Automated SOAR Orchestration:** Direct integration with firewall and EDR APIs (CrowdStrike, SentinelOne) for 1-click endpoint isolation.\n- **Graph Neural Network (GNN) Visualizer:** 3D interactive node-graph mapping global relationships between disparate threat actor campaigns.\n- **Hardware YubiKey Signature Signing:** Cryptographic hardware token signing embedded directly into exported forensic reports.\n- **Live Collaborative Workspace:** Real-time multi-analyst cursor presence and shared investigative scratchpads.\n\n---\n\n# UX Risks & Mitigations\n\n| UX Risk Factor | Operational Hazard | Client-Side Architectural Mitigation |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Automation Bias** | Analysts blindly trusting AI explanations without validating raw evidence. | AI copilot answers are visually isolated, cannot touch verdicts, and must include clickable Evidence IDs linking to raw source bytes. |\n| **Alert Fatigue & Cognitive Blur** | Monotonous dark tables leading to overlooked critical indicators during long shifts. | Multi-density views, strict typographic hierarchy, high-contrast WCAG AA status tokens, and keyboard-driven triage. |\n| **False Sense of Safety** | Low-confidence or degraded cases mistakenly assumed clean by junior analysts. | Strict **Missing Evidence \342\211\240 Safe** rule; dedicated `INCONCLUSIVE` state with explicit Missing Artifact Checklists. |\n| **Context Switching Friction** | Investigators opening 10 browser tabs to check WHOIS, VirusTotal, and GeoIP. | All essential telemetry is enriched and presented natively in unified, defanged tabbed inspectors. |\n| **Legal Inadmissibility** | Reports challenged in court due to unclear provenance or modified timestamps. | Immutable Evidence ID taxonomy, raw EML hash verification, and strict visual separation of deterministic facts from probabilistic AI text. |"
      replacement_content: "# MVP Scope\n\nThe Minimum Viable Product (MVP) for the SIH 2026 PS 26106 evaluation is focused on core triage velocity and forensic depth:\n- **Core Triage Inbox:** Virtualized table, multi-parameter filtering, quick-peek slideout drawer.\n- **Case Workspace HUD:** Real-time Verdict, Risk gauge, Confidence meter, and Envelope metadata.\n- **RFC 5322 Header Forensics:** Complete Received hop visualizer, transit latency delta calculator, and SPF/DKIM/DMARC matrix.\n- **URL & Domain Analysis:** Defanged link viewer, unshortened redirect chain flow, and homoglyph punycode detection.\n- **Infrastructure & Geolocation:** Origin IP ASN/ISP details and interactive dark-canvas world map route.\n- **Attachment Forensics:** Static metadata, double-extension warning, Shannon entropy gauge, and file hash copying.\n- **Evidence Explorer:** Filterable repository of all `EVD-***` items with one-click deep inspector drawer.\n- **Dedicated Forensic Report View:** In-app report review with explicit visual isolation between System Findings and AI Explanations.\n- **Evidentiary AI Assistant:** Side-dock copilot strictly grounded in Evidence IDs with prompt starters.\n- **First-Class INCONCLUSIVE State:** Dedicated UI for low-confidence or degraded signal cases.\n- **Sober Cybersecurity Design System:** WCAG AA compliant dark palette, zero neon gradients, full keyboard navigation.\n\n---\n\n# Future Scope\n\nThe post-hackathon enterprise roadmap addresses enterprise SOC scalability:\n- **Automated SOAR Orchestration:** Direct integration with firewall and EDR APIs (CrowdStrike, SentinelOne) for 1-click endpoint isolation.\n- **Graph Neural Network (GNN) Visualizer:** 3D interactive node-graph mapping global relationships between disparate threat actor campaigns.\n- **Hardware YubiKey Signature Signing:** Cryptographic hardware token signing embedded directly into exported forensic reports.\n- **Live Collaborative Workspace:** Real-time multi-analyst cursor presence and shared investigative scratchpads.\n\n---\n\n# UX Risks\n\n| UX Risk Factor | Operational Hazard | Client-Side Architectural Mitigation |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Automation Bias** | Analysts blindly trusting AI explanations without validating raw evidence. | AI copilot answers are visually isolated, cannot touch verdicts, and must include clickable Evidence IDs linking to raw source bytes. |\n| **Alert Fatigue & Cognitive Blur** | Monotonous dark tables leading to overlooked critical indicators during long shifts. | Multi-density views, strict typographic hierarchy, high-contrast WCAG AA status tokens, and keyboard-driven triage. |\n| **False Sense of Safety** | Low-confidence or degraded cases mistakenly assumed clean by junior analysts. | Strict **Missing Evidence \342\211\240 Safe** rule; dedicated `INCONCLUSIVE` state with explicit Missing Artifact Checklists. |\n| **Context Switching Friction** | Investigators opening 10 browser tabs to check WHOIS, VirusTotal, and GeoIP. | All essential telemetry is enriched and presented natively in unified, defanged tabbed inspectors. |\n| **Legal Inadmissibility** | Reports challenged in court due to unclear provenance or modified timestamps. | Immutable Evidence ID taxonomy, raw EML hash verification, and strict visual separation of deterministic facts from probabilistic AI text. |"
    }
    diff {
      end_line: 1089
      unified_diff {
        lines {
          text: "# ASHIELDER \342\200\224 Frontend Product Specification"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "## AI-Powered Email Threat Detection, GeoLocation & Forensic Intelligence Platform"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Smart India Hackathon 2026 | Problem Statement: PS 26106**  "
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Document Class:** Client-Side Product Experience & Forensic Workstation Architecture  "
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Author:** Senior Product Designer, UX Architect & Cybersecurity SOC UX Specialist  "
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "**Status:** Authoritative Specification | Target Release: Production v1.0  "
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "---"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "# Executive Summary"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 1.1 Problem Statement & Operational Reality (SIH 2026 PS 26106)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "Modern email threats have evolved beyond crude phishing templates into multi-stage, infrastructure-backed cyber operations. Security Operations Center (SOC) analysts, incident responders, and digital forensics examiners confront thousands of inbound alerts daily, including:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Business Email Compromise (BEC) and executive impersonation utilizing deceptive display names and lookalike domains."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Sophisticated multi-hop relay spoofing, DKIM replay attacks, and SPF alignment bypasses."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Weaponized attachments featuring obfuscated macros, polyglot files, and zero-day payloads."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Evasive redirect chains, homograph attacks, punycode manipulation, and conditional geofencing."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "The bottleneck in contemporary security operations is no longer raw detection capability; it is **cognitive bandwidth and investigative velocity**. Analysts are overwhelmed by disjointed tools, fragmented logs, ambiguous risk scores, and AI solutions that hallucinate explanations without verifiable provenance."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 1.2 Product Vision: The ASHIELDER Workstation"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "**ASHIELDER** is an integrated, client-side cybersecurity investigation workstation purpose-built for high-pressure security teams. It bridges the gap between high-throughput automated triage and court-admissible forensic scrutiny."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "ASHIELDER is conceived as:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "$$\\text{Professional SOC Platform} + \\text{Digital Forensics Workstation} + \\text{Modern Enterprise Dashboard} + \\text{Grounded AI Copilot}$$"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "It delivers a unified cockpit where:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "1. An analyst can comprehend an email alert\'s full operational picture within **5 seconds**."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "2. An investigator can drill down into byte-level RFC 5322 header traces, DNS provenance, and sandbox artifacts within **1 click**."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "3. An incident response lead can generate a cryptographically verifiable, audit-ready forensic report within **30 seconds**."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "4. An AI assistant acts strictly as an evidentiary co-pilot, citing immutable Evidence IDs for every conclusion while **never** having write access to verdicts or scores."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 1.3 Target User Spectrum"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Tier-1 SOC Analysts:** Focused on queue velocity, rapid triage, false-positive elimination, and SLA adherence (< 90 seconds per alert)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Tier-2 / Tier-3 Cybersecurity Analysts & Incident Responders:** Focused on deep artifact pivoting, blast radius assessment, root-cause correlation, and enterprise containment."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Digital Forensic Investigators & Law Enforcement / CERT Teams:** Focused on strict chain of custody, uncorrupted header forensics, network transit reconstruction, and legally admissible reports."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Enterprise CISOs & SOC Managers:** Focused on fleet threat posture, recurring campaign attribution, and team operational efficacy."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 1.4 Architecture Stance: Client-Side Forensic Workstation"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "In accordance with system boundaries:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- The backend services (parsing pipelines, ML classification engines, geo-IP lookup databases, sandboxes, vector stores) are developed independently."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- This specification dictates the **entire client-side product experience**, UI state machines, design systems, forensic workflows, accessibility rules, and cognitive load optimizations."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- The client acts as a contract-driven, reactive presentation and analysis layer that treats backend outputs with cryptographic integrity, verifying hashes and rendering evidence without mutation."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "---"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "# User Personas"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| Dimension | Persona 1: SOC Analyst L1 (Triage) | Persona 2: Incident Responder L2/L3 | Persona 3: Digital Forensics Examiner | Persona 4: SOC Manager / CISO |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Representative Archetype** | \"Priya\" \342\200\224 Junior SOC Triage Specialist | \"Arjun\" \342\200\224 Senior Incident Response Engineer | \"Dr. Mehta\" \342\200\224 Digital Forensics & Legal Expert | \"Vikram\" \342\200\224 Head of Cyber Defense |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Primary Objective** | Clear inbox queues rapidly without missing true positives; avoid false alerts. | Identify threat actor infrastructure, isolate affected accounts, stop lateral spread. | Establish legal admissibility, verify RFC 5322 raw signatures, maintain chain of custody. | Monitor threat trends, evaluate team response times, approve enterprise containment actions. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Time Spent Per Case** | 30 to 120 seconds. | 15 minutes to 4 hours. | Hours to days. | 3 to 5 minutes (Executive reviews). |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Key UX Need** | Instant verdict clarity, low visual noise, keyboard triage shortcuts, one-click escalation. | Deep cross-correlation, defanged sandbox artifacts, visual IP hops, similarity search. | Raw byte inspection, cryptographic hash verification, chronological hop latency validation. | High-level risk distribution, campaign impact, one-click court/executive report generation. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Frustrations** | Ambiguous risk scores; hidden context; tools that take 30 seconds to render data. | AI tools that hallucinate reasons without showing underlying headers or URLs. | Reports that cannot be exported to court-compliant PDF; missing raw RFC 822 logs. | Flawed metrics; confusing severity scales where \"low confidence\" is disguised as \"safe\". |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| **Critical Workstation Requirement** | High-contrast visual hierarchy, predictable status badges, rapid case filtering. | Split-screen evidence inspection, interactive GeoIP transit maps, defanged URL redirects. | Hex/Text viewer, RFC 5322 hop tree, cryptographic report signing hashes, immutable evidence IDs. | Executive summary tab, campaign clustering, exportable formal documentation. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "---"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "# Design Principles"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "The ASHIELDER user interface strictly adheres to ten non-negotiable architectural axioms:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "|                                  ASHIELDER CORE DESIGN AXIOMS                                 |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "+------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 1. EVIDENCE FIRST                  | Every claim must directly link to an immutable artifact. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 2. SUMMARY BEFORE DETAIL           | Reveal state in tiers: HUD -> Summary -> Deep Forensics. |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 3. CURRENT CASE \342\211\240 HISTORICAL       | Historical data informs context; it never replaces facts.|"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 4. SYSTEM FINDING \342\211\240 AI EXPLANATION | Deterministic signatures and generative AI never merge.  |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 5. RISK \342\211\240 CONFIDENCE               | Risk is impact/threat; Confidence is evidence fidelity.  |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 6. MISSING EVIDENCE \342\211\240 SAFE         | Degraded signals must show caution, never false safety.  |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 7. AI IS ASSISTANT, NOT AUTHORITY  | The machine proposes, contextualizes; analyst decides.   |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 8. EXPLAINABLE INVESTIGATION       | Every pipeline transformation must be step-auditable.    |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 9. TRACEABLE EVIDENCE IDENTIFIERS | All telemetry receives immutable keys ([EVD-HDR-001]).   |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "| 10. DRILL-DOWN PROVENANCE          | 1 click from explanation to exact raw source bytes.      |"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "+------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------+"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "```"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 1. Evidence First"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "Hypotheses and suggestions are meaningless without tangible artifacts. The UI always renders the raw proof (email headers, DNS records, decoded URLs, file hashes) alongside any synthesized conclusions."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 2. Summary Before Detail"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "To prevent cognitive overload, information is layered into three distinct horizons:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Horizon 1 (0\342\200\2233 seconds):** Visual HUD (Verdict, Risk, Confidence, Sender, Threat Type, Primary Action)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Horizon 2 (3\342\200\22330 seconds):** Key Findings Panel, Authentication Matrix, Hop Route, Critical URL/Attachment cards."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **Horizon 3 (Deep Analysis):** Raw Header Hex/Text inspector, Redirect chain hop logs, Passive DNS tables, Execution sandbox graphs."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 3. Current Case \342\211\240 Historical Context"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "Past attacks from a similar domain or IP provide heuristic intelligence, but they **must never** be conflated with the evidentiary facts of the current active message. Historical intel is isolated visually with distinct border treatments, subtle background patterns, and explicit \"HISTORICAL CORRELATION\" labeling."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 4. System Finding \342\211\240 AI Explanation"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "Deterministic findings (e.g., `DKIM signature validation failed: body hash mismatch [RFC 6376]`) are generated by deterministic code. Generative AI summaries are probabilistic language syntheses. "
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **System Findings** are rendered with solid, high-contrast, structured metadata badges and technical monospace codes."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- **AI Explanations** are rendered in dedicated containers with a subtle AI insignia, conversational yet disciplined typography, and mandatory evidentiary footnotes."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 5. Risk \342\211\240 Confidence (The 2D Risk-Confidence Grid)"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "A message can have **100% Risk** with **99% Confidence** (e.g., known ransomware hash matched against multiple threat feeds). Conversely, a message can have **80% Risk** with **20% Confidence** (e.g., brand-new domain registered 10 minutes ago sending an urgent invoice, but external sandbox timed out). Combining these into a single scalar destroys tactical fidelity. ASHIELDER displays Risk and Confidence as distinct orthogonal metrics."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 6. Missing Evidence \342\211\240 Safe"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "If an attachment sandbox times out, or a WHOIS server throttles rate limits, the system does **not** assume the artifact is benign. The UI highlights missing or failed pipeline nodes in distinct amber/neutral warning states, lowering the system\'s **Confidence Score** while keeping the analyst vigilant."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 7. AI is Assistant, not Authority"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "The AI Copilot does **not** possess controls to alter case verdicts, modify risk scores, or trigger irreversible escalations. It assists solely by correlating data, explaining technical RFC nuances, highlighting anomalies, and drafting investigative summaries."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 8. Explainable Investigation Journey"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "Every analysis pipeline step (Ingestion $\\rightarrow$ MIME Unpacking $\\rightarrow$ Header Parsing $\\rightarrow$ DNS Resolution $\\rightarrow$ Sandbox Detonation $\\rightarrow$ Threat Scoring) is visualized in an interactive, chronological **Investigation Journey**. If a tool fails or produces degraded output, the analyst sees exactly where and why."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 9. Traceable Forensic Evidence"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "Every parsed forensic artifact is assigned a globally unique, immutable Evidence ID (e.g., `EVD-HDR-001`, `EVD-NET-014`, `EVD-URL-003`, `EVD-ATT-002`). These identifiers are hyperlinked across all reports, AI responses, and timeline entries."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 10. Single-Click Source Inspection"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "Whenever an analyst reads a conclusion or copilot answer, clicking an Evidence Chip immediately opens the **Evidence Explorer** or **Header Inspector**, scrolling precisely to the raw line or byte range and highlighting the verified source string."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "---"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
