        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 11.1 Security-First Defanging Default"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "All links are displayed **defanged** (`hxxp://`, `[.]`, `[:]`) by default to prevent accidental clicks or browser-triggered pre-fetching. An explicit copy button allows copying either defanged or raw format (with a safety prompt)."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 11.2 Anchor vs Target Mismatch Indicator"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "The UI compares the visual link text displayed to the human recipient against the actual `href` destination. If the text reads `https://legitimate-bank.com` while the link points to `http://evil-tracker.com`, a prominent **Deceptive Anchor Mismatch** warning is triggered."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 11.3 Interactive Redirect Chain Explorer"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "Visualizes each redirection step (HTTP 301, 302, 307, meta-refresh, or JavaScript `window.location`). Displays:"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Response HTTP headers for each hop."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "- Cloaking & Evasion detection: Highlights if redirect targets change based on client user-agent or geographic IP."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "### 11.4 Homograph & Punycode Dissector"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "Detects internationalized domain names (IDN) using Cyrillic, Greek, or lookalike glyphs (e.g., Latin \'a\' substituted with Cyrillic \'\320\260\' `U+0430`). The UI highlights the exact manipulated character in bright warning yellow with the corresponding unicode codepoint."
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
