  planner_response {
    response: "# ASHIELDER \342\200\224 Frontend Product Specification Complete\n\nThe authoritative client-side product specification for **ASHIELDER** (*AI-Powered Email Threat Detection, GeoLocation & Forensic Intelligence Platform*, **SIH 2026 PS 26106**) has been authored and established at `/ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md`.\n\nIn strict adherence to your instructions:\n- **Zero code was written or modified** in the application codebase.\n- **Zero backend APIs or server endpoints were invented**.\n- The entire specification is structured to govern the **client-side product experience**, UI state machines, cognitive load hierarchies, evidence provenance architectures, and human-computer interactions.\n\n---\n\n### Architectural & Design Highlights of the Specification\n\n- **The Sober Forensic Aesthetic:** Explicitly rejects \"AI slop\", neon cyber-glow, gamified HUDs, and generic SaaS card clutter. Specifies an obsidian-and-slate neutral foundation (`#0A0D14` base, `#111622` surface) with WCAG 2.1 AA compliant color tokens and monospaced typography (`JetBrains Mono` / `IBM Plex Mono`) for all forensic telemetry.\n- **5-Second Cognitive Comprehension Rule:** Organizes information into three strict visibility horizons:\n  1. *Horizon 1 (0\342\200\2233s):* Persistent Case HUD featuring the independent 2D **Risk Gauge** ($0-100$) and **Confidence Meter** ($0-100$), Verdict Badge, Envelope Metadata, and Primary Action Toolbar.\n  2. *Horizon 2 (3\342\200\22330s):* Key Evidentiary Findings, 5-pillar Authentication Validation Matrix (SPF, DKIM, DMARC, ARC, BIMI), and Chronological Received Hop Route with transit latency deltas.\n  3. *Horizon 3 (Deep Analysis):* Defanged URL redirect chains, homograph punycode dissector, sovereign jurisdiction map, high-entropy attachment analysis, and raw RFC 5322 header/hex inspectors.\n- **Strict Visual Separation of Powers:**\n  - **`SYSTEM FINDING` vs `AI EXPLANATION`:** Deterministic parser signatures are rendered in high-contrast slate tables with monospace RFC citations. Probabilistic AI summaries are isolated in distinct copilot containers with mandatory evidentiary footnotes.\n  - **`CURRENT CASE` vs `HISTORICAL CONTEXT`:** Past campaigns and vector similarity matches are isolated with distinct boundaries and explicit disclaimers so past alerts cannot be mistaken for current physical evidence.\n  - **`RISK` vs `CONFIDENCE`:** Separated orthogonally so low-confidence or degraded signal states cannot masquerade as \"safe\".\n  - **`INCONCLUSIVE` as a First-Class State:** Dedicated state with a **Missing Artifact Checklist** outlining exact manual triage protocols when external tools time out or payloads are encrypted.\n- **Traceable Evidence Taxonomy (`EVD-***`):** Every artifact across headers, network hops, URLs, and attachments receives an immutable identifier (e.g., `[EVD-HDR-001]`, `[EVD-URL-004]`), hyperlinked for single-click provenance drill-down to raw source bytes.\n- **Grounded AI Copilot:** Strictly governed as an evidentiary assistant without write permissions to alter verdicts or risk scores, bound to cite evidence IDs for every assertion.\n- **Court-Admissible Forensic Report Engine:** Formatted with cryptographic SHA-256 dossier hashes, examiner statement blocks, tool failure disclosures, and chain-of-custody audit seals.\n\n---\n\n### Complete Specification Sections Created in `ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md`\n\n1. `# Executive Summary`\n2. `# User Personas`\n3. `# Design Principles`\n4. `# Information Architecture`\n5. `# Navigation`\n6. `# Case Inbox`\n7. `# Case Workspace`\n8. `# Investigation View`\n9. `# Evidence Explorer`\n10. `# Header Forensics`\n11. `# URL Analysis`\n12. `# Infrastructure Intelligence`\n13. `# Geolocation`\n14. `# Attachments`\n15. `# Historical Intelligence`\n16. `# Re-investigation`\n17. `# Forensic Report`\n18. `# AI Assistant`\n19. `# Error States`\n20. `# Loading States`\n21. `# Empty States`\n22. `# INCONCLUSIVE State`\n23. `# Authentication UX`\n24. `# RBAC-ready UX`\n25. `# Accessibility`\n26. `# Responsive Strategy`\n27. `# Design System`\n28. `# Component Inventory` (32 purpose-built forensic components cataloged)\n29. `# Page Inventory`\n30. `# User Journeys` (4 real-world operational workflows detailed step-by-step)\n31. `# MVP Scope` (SIH 2026 PS 26106 target deliverables)\n32. `# Future Scope`\n33. `# UX Risks`\n34. `# Final Recommendations`\n\nThe document at `/ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md` stands ready to serve as the single source of truth for engineering implementation and SIH 2026 project defense."
    thinking: "**Verifying User Request**\n\nI\'ve got good news! Both `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` are flawless. Now, I\'m cross-referencing the required sections and content specified in `ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md` against every single detail of the user request. So far, the focus is on confirming our project\'s scope: building ASHIELDER, with AI-Powered Email Threat Detection, Geo integration and more.\n\n\n**Defining Client Experience**\n\nI\'ve nailed down the core user base: SOC analysts, investigators, and security teams. The client-side focus is crystal clear \342\200\223 no backend invention is needed. The design principles are locked in; emphasizing evidence, summaries, and explainability is key. Also, I\'ve got a firm grasp on the required UI aesthetic and am starting to think of a high-fidelity representation of the product.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "# ASHIELDER \342\200\224 Frontend Product Specification Complete\n\nThe authoritative client-side product specification for **ASHIELDER** (*AI-Powered Email Threat Detection, GeoLocation & Forensic Intelligence Platform*, **SIH 2026 PS 26106**) has been authored and established at `/ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md`.\n\nIn strict adherence to your instructions:\n- **Zero code was written or modified** in the application codebase.\n- **Zero backend APIs or server endpoints were invented**.\n- The entire specification is structured to govern the **client-side product experience**, UI state machines, cognitive load hierarchies, evidence provenance architectures, and human-computer interactions.\n\n---\n\n### Architectural & Design Highlights of the Specification\n\n- **The Sober Forensic Aesthetic:** Explicitly rejects \"AI slop\", neon cyber-glow, gamified HUDs, and generic SaaS card clutter. Specifies an obsidian-and-slate neutral foundation (`#0A0D14` base, `#111622` surface) with WCAG 2.1 AA compliant color tokens and monospaced typography (`JetBrains Mono` / `IBM Plex Mono`) for all forensic telemetry.\n- **5-Second Cognitive Comprehension Rule:** Organizes information into three strict visibility horizons:\n  1. *Horizon 1 (0\342\200\2233s):* Persistent Case HUD featuring the independent 2D **Risk Gauge** ($0-100$) and **Confidence Meter** ($0-100$), Verdict Badge, Envelope Metadata, and Primary Action Toolbar.\n  2. *Horizon 2 (3\342\200\22330s):* Key Evidentiary Findings, 5-pillar Authentication Validation Matrix (SPF, DKIM, DMARC, ARC, BIMI), and Chronological Received Hop Route with transit latency deltas.\n  3. *Horizon 3 (Deep Analysis):* Defanged URL redirect chains, homograph punycode dissector, sovereign jurisdiction map, high-entropy attachment analysis, and raw RFC 5322 header/hex inspectors.\n- **Strict Visual Separation of Powers:**\n  - **`SYSTEM FINDING` vs `AI EXPLANATION`:** Deterministic parser signatures are rendered in high-contrast slate tables with monospace RFC citations. Probabilistic AI summaries are isolated in distinct copilot containers with mandatory evidentiary footnotes.\n  - **`CURRENT CASE` vs `HISTORICAL CONTEXT`:** Past campaigns and vector similarity matches are isolated with distinct boundaries and explicit disclaimers so past alerts cannot be mistaken for current physical evidence.\n  - **`RISK` vs `CONFIDENCE`:** Separated orthogonally so low-confidence or degraded signal states cannot masquerade as \"safe\".\n  - **`INCONCLUSIVE` as a First-Class State:** Dedicated state with a **Missing Artifact Checklist** outlining exact manual triage protocols when external tools time out or payloads are encrypted.\n- **Traceable Evidence Taxonomy (`EVD-***`):** Every artifact across headers, network hops, URLs, and attachments receives an immutable identifier (e.g., `[EVD-HDR-001]`, `[EVD-URL-004]`), hyperlinked for single-click provenance drill-down to raw source bytes.\n- **Grounded AI Copilot:** Strictly governed as an evidentiary assistant without write permissions to alter verdicts or risk scores, bound to cite evidence IDs for every assertion.\n- **Court-Admissible Forensic Report Engine:** Formatted with cryptographic SHA-256 dossier hashes, examiner statement blocks, tool failure disclosures, and chain-of-custody audit seals.\n\n---\n\n### Complete Specification Sections Created in `ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md`\n\n1. `# Executive Summary`\n2. `# User Personas`\n3. `# Design Principles`\n4. `# Information Architecture`\n5. `# Navigation`\n6. `# Case Inbox`\n7. `# Case Workspace`\n8. `# Investigation View`\n9. `# Evidence Explorer`\n10. `# Header Forensics`\n11. `# URL Analysis`\n12. `# Infrastructure Intelligence`\n13. `# Geolocation`\n14. `# Attachments`\n15. `# Historical Intelligence`\n16. `# Re-investigation`\n17. `# Forensic Report`\n18. `# AI Assistant`\n19. `# Error States`\n20. `# Loading States`\n21. `# Empty States`\n22. `# INCONCLUSIVE State`\n23. `# Authentication UX`\n24. `# RBAC-ready UX`\n25. `# Accessibility`\n26. `# Responsive Strategy`\n27. `# Design System`\n28. `# Component Inventory` (32 purpose-built forensic components cataloged)\n29. `# Page Inventory`\n30. `# User Journeys` (4 real-world operational workflows detailed step-by-step)\n31. `# MVP Scope` (SIH 2026 PS 26106 target deliverables)\n32. `# Future Scope`\n33. `# UX Risks`\n34. `# Final Recommendations`\n\nThe document at `/ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md` stands ready to serve as the single source of truth for engineering implementation and SIH 2026 project defense."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
