  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Project Documentation**\n\nI\'m now focused on generating `ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_API_INTEGRATION_SPEC.md` for STAGE 2 of the ASHIELDER frontend. Currently, I\'m carefully examining the prompt instructions, available backend execution traces, audit reports, and the runtime matrix. This careful analysis is crucial.\n\n\n**Analyzing Backend E2E Traces**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously examining the \"ASHIELDER Backend E2E Trace\" data, including actual files, routes, tools, and contracts for Phases 2 and 4. I\'m focusing on the different case scenarios (benign, phishing, BEC, attachment, historical match, tool failure, resource exhaustion, and inconclusive cases) along with the Backend Runtime Matrix\'s endpoints like `/health`, `/api/v1/emails/analyze`, and `/api/v1/investigations/analyze`.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoint Behavior**\n\nI\'m now detailing the behavior of specific endpoints. I\'ve documented `/api/v1/investigations/{id}/report` and the `POST /api/v1/investigations/{id}/reinvestigate` endpoint which is part of Phase 3/4, noting its case ID lineage. I\'m taking care to clarify CORS configuration and rate limiting, including the implementation details. Finally, I\'ve outlined the global error handling, request ID handling and data storage methods.\n\n\n**Clarifying Async/Sync Patterns**\n\nI\'m currently detailing the API interaction patterns. It\'s synchronous HTTP request-response. Groq LLM reasoning is disabled in the automated pipeline. The `GET /report` endpoint uses Groq optionally, falling back to a deterministic summary if unavailable. RBAC is deferred, using a single shared API key.\n\n\n**Defining Project Boundaries**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the MVP boundary, the Backend Gaps (ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_BACKEND_GAPS), the Security Boundary, and the Final API Contract Table, specifically in Section 14, 15, 16, and 17. I\'m leveraging the `InvestigationResult`, `ParsedEmail`, `EmailEvidencePackage`, and `EvidenceItem` types, and the `EvidenceType`, `SourceType`, `StopReason`, `AttackHypothesisType`, and `Verdict` enum fields and values from the existing codebase and traces.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_414280"
      name: "create_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Content\":\"# ASHIELDER \342\200\224 Frontend API Integration Specification\\n## Contract-Driven Client-to-Backend Integration Architecture\\n**Smart India Hackathon 2026 | Problem Statement: PS 26106**  \\n**Document Class:** Client-Side API Integration Specification & Technical Contract  \\n**Source of Truth:** ASHIELDER Backend Runtime Traces, FastAPI Routing, and Contract Audits (Phase 1\342\200\223Phase 4)  \\n**Status:** Authoritative Specification | Target Release: Production v1.0  \\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 1 \342\200\224 BACKEND API INVENTORY\\n\\nThis inventory catalog represents the complete, verified surface of the ASHIELDER backend API (`app/main.py`, `app/api/v1/investigation.py`, `app/api/v1/email.py`). Every endpoint, path parameter, header, request schema, and response contract reflects the actual runtime behavior verified during Phase 4 validation.\\n\\n### 1.1 Endpoint Overview Matrix\\n\\n| # | Endpoint Name | Method | Path | Auth Mechanism | Rate Limited | Status |\\n| :- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **EP-01** | Health Check | `GET` | `/health` | None | No | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED (200 OK) |\\n| **EP-02** | Analyze Email (Investigation) | `POST` | `/api/v1/investigations/analyze` | `X-API-Key` | Yes (10/min) | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED |\\n| **EP-03** | Get Investigation Details | `GET` | `/api/v1/investigations/{id}` | `X-API-Key` | Yes (10/min) | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED |\\n| **EP-04** | Get Investigation Evidence | `GET` | `/api/v1/investigations/{id}/evidence` | `X-API-Key` | Yes (10/min) | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED |\\n| **EP-05** | Get Investigation Report | `GET` | `/api/v1/investigations/{id}/report` | `X-API-Key` | Yes (10/min) | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED |\\n| **EP-06** | Re-investigate Case | `POST` | `/api/v1/investigations/{id}/reinvestigate` | `X-API-Key` | Yes (10/min) | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED |\\n| **EP-07** | Parse Email Only | `POST` | `/api/v1/emails/analyze` | Bearer Token (Firebase) | No | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1.2 Exhaustive Endpoint Technical Specifications\\n\\n#### EP-01: Health Check\\n- **Path:** `GET /health`\\n- **Purpose:** System readiness, container liveness, and uptime monitoring.\\n- **Authentication:** `None`.\\n- **Required Headers:** None (Optional: `X-Request-ID`).\\n- **Request Parameters / Body:** None.\\n- **Response Schema:**\\n  ```json\\n  {\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"healthy\\\"\\n  }\\n  ```\\n- **HTTP Status Codes:** `200 OK`.\\n- **Timeout Consideration:** 2,000 ms.\\n- **Frontend Consumer:** Global App Shell, Network Connection Health Ping, Offline Banner.\\n- **Backend Status:** \342\234\205 Fully Implemented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### EP-02: Analyze Email (Full Forensic Investigation)\\n- **Path:** `POST /api/v1/investigations/analyze`\\n- **File & Function:** `app/api/v1/investigation.py:analyze_email()`\\n- **Purpose:** Primary entry point for email triage. Ingests a raw RFC 822/5322 `.eml` file, triggers synchronous multi-level adaptive investigation (L0 deterministic $\\\\rightarrow$ L1 ML $\\\\rightarrow$ L2 external enrichment), calculates Risk and Confidence, assigns a Verdict with stop-guards, and persists case artifacts.\\n- **Authentication:** `X-API-Key: <SECRET_KEY>` enforced via FastAPI dependency `Depends(verify_api_key)`.\\n- **Required Headers:**\\n  - `X-API-Key`: Secret API key matching backend `settings.SECRET_KEY`.\\n  - `Content-Type`: `multipart/form-data`.\\n  - `X-Request-ID` (Optional but recommended): Client-generated UUIDv4 for distributed tracing.\\n- **Request Body (Multipart Form):**\\n  - `file`: Binary file stream of the `.eml` email message.\\n  - **Validation Constraints:** Filename required (must end with `.eml` or be valid MIME), body cannot be 0 bytes, maximum size limit enforced at 10 MB (10,485,760 bytes).\\n- **Response Schema (`InvestigationResult` contract from `app/contracts/result.py`):**\\n  ```json\\n  {\\n    \\\"case_id\\\": \\\"case_20260905_181402_a1b2c3d4\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"STOPPED\\\",\\n    \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"MALICIOUS\\\",\\n    \\\"risk_score\\\": 92.5,\\n    \\\"confidence\\\": 0.842,\\n    \\\"stop_reason\\\": \\\"CONFIDENCE_TARGET_REACHED\\\",\\n    \\\"iteration_count\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"evidence_count\\\": 42,\\n    \\\"evidence_ids\\\": [\\n      \\\"EVD-HDR-001\\\",\\n      \\\"EVD-AUT-002\\\",\\n      \\\"EVD-NET-003\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"hypotheses\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"hypothesis_type\\\": \\\"credential_phishing\\\",\\n        \\\"score\\\": 0.88,\\n        \\\"active\\\": true\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \\\"hypothesis_type\\\": \\\"spoofing\\\",\\n        \\\"score\\\": 0.92,\\n        \\\"active\\\": true\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"budget\\\": {\\n      \\\"tool_calls_used\\\": 7,\\n      \\\"max_tool_calls\\\": 16,\\n      \\\"external_calls_used\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"max_external_calls\\\": 6,\\n      \\\"latency_ms_used\\\": 1842.4,\\n      \\\"max_latency_ms\\\": 4000.0,\\n      \\\"llm_tokens_used\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"max_llm_tokens\\\": 0\\n    },\\n    \\\"tools_used\\\": [\\n      \\\"spf_dkim_dmarc\\\",\\n      \\\"header_parse\\\",\\n      \\\"relay_reconstruction\\\",\\n      \\\"deterministic_heuristics\\\",\\n      \\\"url_canonicalizer\\\",\\n      \\\"ip_classifier\\\",\\n      \\\"nlp_intent_ml\\\",\\n      \\\"url_ml\\\",\\n      \\\"geoip_lookup\\\",\\n      \\\"sender_history\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"tools_failed\\\": [],\\n    \\\"missing_evidence\\\": [],\\n    \\\"geolocation\\\": {\\n      \\\"origin_ip\\\": \\\"185.220.101.5\\\",\\n      \\\"country\\\": \\\"Russian Federation\\\",\\n      \\\"country_code\\\": \\\"RU\\\",\\n      \\\"city\\\": \\\"Saint Petersburg\\\",\\n      \\\"latitude\\\": 59.9343,\\n      \\\"longitude\\\": 30.3351,\\n      \\\"asn\\\": \\\"AS208323\\\",\\n      \\\"isp\\\": \\\"Tor Exit Network\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"content_analysis\\\": {\\n      \\\"intent_label\\\": \\\"PHISHING\\\",\\n      \\\"intent_confidence\\\": 0.892,\\n      \\\"urgency_score\\\": 0.85,\\n      \\\"social_engineering_flags\\\": [\\n        \\\"urgency\\\",\\n        \\\"fear_trigger\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"mentioned_organizations\\\": [\\n        \\\"Bank of America\\\",\\n        \\\"Microsoft\\\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \\\"audit_chain_last_hash\\\": \\\"a8f3b24c9e81d2f0a1c3e4b5d6f7890123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01\\\"\\n  }\\n  ```\\n- **Error Schema (`app/main.py` global error handler):**\\n  ```json\\n  {\\n    \\\"error\\\": {\\n      \\\"code\\\": \\\"VALIDATION_ERROR\\\",\\n      \\\"message\\\": \\\"File is empty or missing valid RFC 822 payload.\\\",\\n      \\\"request_id\\\": \\\"req_88f1a23c-9b12-4f32\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n  ```\\n- **Expected HTTP Status Codes:**\\n  - `200 OK`: Successful analysis and verdict generated.\\n  - `400 Bad Request`: Empty file, invalid MIME headers, or 0-byte payload.\\n  - `401 Unauthorized`: Missing or invalid `X-API-Key`.\\n  - `413 Payload Too Large`: Upload exceeds 10 MB limit.\\n  - `422 Unprocessable Entity`: Multipart form parsing failure or invalid field key.\\n  - `429 Too Many Requests`: Client IP exceeded 10 req/min rate limit.\\n  - `500 Internal Server Error`: Unhandled parser/engine crash (wrapped in structured error JSON).\\n- **Timeout Considerations:** 8,000 ms client-side timeout (backend internal budget allows up to 4,000 ms tool latency plus model/DB overhead).\\n- **Frontend Consumer:** Ingestion Dropzone, Case Workspace Creator, Fast Triage Modal.\\n- **Backend Status:** \342\234\205 Fully Implemented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### EP-03: Get Investigation Details\\n- **Path:** `GET /api/v1/investigations/{investigation_id}`\\n- **Purpose:** Retrieve a previously executed investigation by its unique `case_id`.\\n- **Authentication:** `X-API-Key: <SECRET_KEY>`.\\n- **Required Headers:** `X-API-Key`, `X-Request-ID`.\\n- **Path Parameters:** `investigation_id` (string, e.g., `case_20260905_181402_a1b2c3d4`).\\n- **Response Schema:** Returns the `InvestigationResult` model matching EP-02, supplemented with database timestamps (`created_at`, `updated_at`).\\n- **Status Codes:** `200 OK`, `401 Unauthorized`, `404 Not Found`, `429 Too Many Requests`, `500 Internal Server Error`.\\n- **Backend Status:** \342\234\205 Fully Implemented (backed by SQLite in local/test and Supabase PostgreSQL in staging/prod).\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### EP-04: Get Investigation Evidence\\n- **Path:** `GET /api/v1/investigations/{investigation_id}/evidence`\\n- **Purpose:** Fetches the full normalized list of typed `EvidenceItem` records collected across all investigation levels.\\n- **Authentication:** `X-API-Key: <SECRET_KEY>`.\\n- **Required Headers:** `X-API-Key`, `X-Request-ID`.\\n- **Path Parameters:** `investigation_id` (string).\\n- **Response Schema:** Array of serialized `EvidenceItem` objects:\\n  ```json\\n  [\\n    {\\n      \\\"evidence_id\\\": \\\"EVD-AUT-001\\\",\\n      \\\"case_id\\\": \\\"case_20260905_181402_a1b2c3d4\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence_type\\\": \\\"FACT\\\",\\n      \\\"category\\\": \\\"AUTHENTICATION\\\",\\n      \\\"key\\\": \\\"auth_dmarc_result\\\",\\n      \\\"value\\\": \\\"fail\\\",\\n      \\\"source_type\\\": \\\"PARSER\\\",\\n      \\\"producer\\\": \\\"spf_dkim_dmarc\\\",\\n      \\\"provenance\\\": {\\n        \\\"file_offset\\\": 1024,\\n        \\\"rfc_header\\\": \\\"Authentication-Results\\\",\\n        \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-09-05T18:14:02.124Z\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": 1.0,\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"CRITICAL\\\",\\n      \\\"raw_json\\\": {\\n        \\\"domain\\\": \\\"bankofamerica-secure.net\\\",\\n        \\\"policy\\\": \\\"reject\\\",\\n        \\\"alignment\\\": \\\"fail\\\"\\n      }\\n    }\\n  ]\\n  ```\\n- **Status Codes:** `200 OK`, `401 Unauthorized`, `404 Not Found`, `500 Internal Server Error`.\\n- **Frontend Consumer:** Evidence Explorer tab, Forensic Deep Inspector, Header Forensics matrix.\\n- **Backend Status:** \342\234\205 Fully Implemented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### EP-05: Get Investigation Report\\n- **Path:** `GET /api/v1/investigations/{investigation_id}/report`\\n- **Purpose:** Generates or retrieves an audit-ready, structured forensic report containing executive summary, evidence breakdowns, tool execution audit, and Groq LLM narrative (or deterministic fallback narrative if Groq is unconfigured).\\n- **Authentication:** `X-API-Key: <SECRET_KEY>`.\\n- **Required Headers:** `X-API-Key`, `X-Request-ID`.\\n- **Path Parameters:** `investigation_id` (string).\\n- **Response Schema:**\\n  ```json\\n  {\\n    \\\"case_id\\\": \\\"case_20260905_181402_a1b2c3d4\\\",\\n    \\\"generated_at\\\": \\\"2026-09-05T18:14:04.912Z\\\",\\n    \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"MALICIOUS\\\",\\n    \\\"risk_score\\\": 92.5,\\n    \\\"confidence\\\": 0.842,\\n    \\\"case_summary\\\": {\\n      \\\"sender\\\": \\\"security@bankofamerica-secure.net\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\": \\\"URGENT: Verify Your Account Access\\\",\\n      \\\"received_time\\\": \\\"2026-09-05T18:13:58Z\\\",\\n      \\\"total_evidence_collected\\\": 42\\n    },\\n    \\\"evidence_summary\\\": {\\n      \\\"facts_count\\\": 22,\\n      \\\"heuristics_count\\\": 14,\\n      \\\"ml_signals_count\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"threat_intel_count\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"historical_count\\\": 0\\n    },\\n    \\\"evidence_by_type\\\": {\\n      \\\"FACT\\\": [...],\\n      \\\"HEURISTIC\\\": [...],\\n      \\\"ML_SIGNAL\\\": [...],\\n      \\\"THREAT_INTEL\\\": [...]\\n    },\\n    \\\"deterministic_summary\\\": \\\"Investigation evaluated 42 items of evidence across 3 iterations. DMARC, SPF, and DKIM authentication failed for the origin domain bankofamerica-secure.net. Content intent classifier detected PHISHING with 89.2% confidence. Origin IP 185.220.101.5 is an active Tor Exit relay.\\\",\\n    \\\"groq_narrative\\\": null,\\n    \\\"groq_status\\\": \\\"GROQ_UNAVAILABLE\\\",\\n    \\\"geolocation\\\": {\\n      \\\"origin_ip\\\": \\\"185.220.101.5\\\",\\n      \\\"country\\\": \\\"Russian Federation\\\",\\n      \\\"asn\\\": \\\"AS208323\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"content_analysis\\\": {\\n      \\\"intent_label\\\": \\\"PHISHING\\\",\\n      \\\"urgency_score\\\": 0.85\\n    },\\n    \\\"audit_chain\\\": {\\n      \\\"chain_length\\\": 8,\\n      \\\"last_hash\\\": \\\"a8f3b24c9e81d2f0a1c3e4b5d6f7890123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01\\\",\\n      \\\"tamper_detected\\\": false\\n    }\\n  }\\n  ```\\n- **Status Codes:** `200 OK`, `401 Unauthorized`, `404 Not Found`, `500 Internal Server Error`.\\n- **Frontend Consumer:** Forensic Report View, PDF Printing Engine, Legal Audit Export.\\n- **Backend Status:** \342\234\205 Fully Implemented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### EP-06: Re-investigate Case\\n- **Path:** `POST /api/v1/investigations/{investigation_id}/reinvestigate`\\n- **File & Function:** `app/api/v1/investigation.py:reinvestigate_case()`\\n- **Purpose:** Re-executes the full Stage 1 adaptive investigation pipeline against an existing case\'s normalized package. Generates a new case ID with lineage back-reference to `original_case_id`, bypassing cached results.\\n- **Authentication:** `X-API-Key: <SECRET_KEY>`.\\n- **Required Headers:** `X-API-Key`, `Content-Type: application/json`.\\n- **Path Parameters:** `investigation_id` (string).\\n- **Request Body (JSON):**\\n  ```json\\n  {\\n    \\\"reason\\\": \\\"New threat intelligence feeds available for origin IP 185.220.101.5\\\",\\n    \\\"requested_by\\\": \\\"analyst_priya\\\"\\n  }\\n  ```\\n- **Response Schema:** Returns a fresh `InvestigationResult` model (EP-02 schema) where:\\n  - `case_id`: Newly generated case identifier (prefixed with `reinv_` or timestamp UUID).\\n  - `original_case_id`: String containing the target `investigation_id`.\\n  - Evidence list includes a `FACT` item of category `REINVESTIGATION` capturing the trigger reason and timestamp.\\n- **Status Codes:** `200 OK`, `401 Unauthorized`, `404 Not Found`, `422 Unprocessable Entity`.\\n- **Frontend Consumer:** Case Workspace Re-investigate Button, Diff Comparison Modal.\\n- **Backend Status:** \342\234\205 Fully Implemented (upgraded from 501 stub in Phase 3/4).\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### EP-07: Parse Email Only (Lightweight Inspection)\\n- **Path:** `POST /api/v1/emails/analyze`\\n- **Purpose:** Pure MIME header parsing and attachment extraction without running the adaptive investigation loop, ML models, or risk scoring.\\n- **Authentication:** `Authorization: Bearer <FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN>`.\\n- **Required Headers:** `Authorization`, `Content-Type: multipart/form-data`.\\n- **Request Body (Multipart Form):** `file: UploadFile`.\\n- **Response Schema (`ParsedEmail` contract from `app/contracts/email.py`):**\\n  ```json\\n  {\\n    \\\"subject\\\": \\\"URGENT: Verify Your Account Access\\\",\\n    \\\"from_header\\\": \\\"security@bankofamerica-secure.net\\\",\\n    \\\"to_headers\\\": [\\\"victim@targetcorp.in\\\"],\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-09-05T18:13:58Z\\\",\\n    \\\"message_id\\\": \\\"<20260905181358.12345@bankofamerica-secure.net>\\\",\\n    \\\"return_path\\\": \\\"bounce@evil-server.com\\\",\\n    \\\"reply_to\\\": \\\"hacker@freemail.com\\\",\\n    \\\"received_headers\\\": [\\n      \\\"from mail.evil-server.com (185.220.101.5) by mx.targetcorp.in...\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"authentication_results\\\": \\\"spf=fail dkim=fail dmarc=fail...\\\",\\n    \\\"body_plain\\\": \\\"Please verify your wire transfer immediately...\\\",\\n    \\\"body_html\\\": \\\"<p>Please <a href=\'http://bankofamerica-secure.net/verify\'>Click Here</a></p>\\\",\\n    \\\"urls\\\": [\\n      \\\"http://bankofamerica-secure.net/verify?id=12345\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"attachments\\\": [\\n      {\\n        \\\"filename\\\": \\\"Invoice_8812.pdf\\\",\\n        \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\\\",\\n        \\\"content_type\\\": \\\"application/pdf\\\",\\n        \\\"size_bytes\\\": 1488912\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"8f4c391209b124808c1d3298a01f92e4bc18921a9e320489a1c9041289fe1234\\\"\\n  }\\n  ```\\n- **Status Codes:** `200 OK`, `400 Bad Request`, `401 Unauthorized`, `500 Internal Server Error`.\\n- **Frontend Consumer:** Header Raw Inspection Tool, Offline EML Parser utility.\\n- **Backend Status:** \342\234\205 Fully Implemented.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 2 \342\200\224 FRONTEND FEATURE \342\206\222 API MAPPING\\n\\nThis matrix directly maps every functional area defined in Stage 1 (`ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md`) to the actual backend capabilities discovered during Phase 1\342\200\2234 runtime audits.\\n\\n| Frontend Feature | Required API | Backend Status | Data Required | Missing Dependency | Frontend Fallback Strategy |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Authentication** | `POST /api/v1/investigations/*` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | `X-API-Key` | Backend lacks multi-user RBAC. | Store API key in secure client session storage; prompt analyst if unset. |\\n| **Case Inbox / List** | `GET /api/v1/investigations` | \360\237\224\264 NOT IMPLEMENTED | List of cases with pagination | Backend lacks a global `GET /investigations` list endpoint. | Maintain indexed local history of analyzed cases in browser IndexedDB/LocalStorage. |\\n| **Case Filtering / Search** | Client-side query engine | \360\237\237\241 PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED | Filter parameters | No backend search endpoint exists. | Filter client-side against the local case cache and loaded investigation results. |\\n| **Case Workspace HUD** | `POST /analyze` or `GET /{id}` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | `case_id`, `verdict`, `risk_score`, `confidence` | None. | Direct binding to `InvestigationResult`. |\\n| **EML Ingestion** | `POST /api/v1/investigations/analyze` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | Multipart Form `.eml` | None. | Direct binding to standard browser `FormData` file upload. |\\n| **Investigation Journey** | `InvestigationResult.budget`, `tools_used`, `tools_failed` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | Step progression telemetry | Granular per-step timestamps are aggregated, not individual step objects. | Derive journey steps deterministically from `tools_used`, `tools_failed`, and `iteration_count`. |\\n| **Risk / Confidence / Verdict** | `InvestigationResult` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | `risk_score`, `confidence`, `verdict` | None. | Direct binding to 2D Risk-Confidence HUD widgets. |\\n| **Key Findings** | `GET /{id}/evidence` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | Highest weighted `EvidenceItem` records | None. | Filter evidence where `severity == \'CRITICAL\' \\\\|\\\\| \'HIGH\'` or score weight $\\\\ge 20$. |\\n| **Evidence Explorer** | `GET /api/v1/investigations/{id}/evidence` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | Full array of `EvidenceItem` | None. | Render filterable, sortable forensic datatable. |\\n| **Header Forensics Matrix** | `GET /{id}/evidence` & `POST /emails/analyze` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | `FACT` items from `spf_dkim_dmarc`, `header_parse` | None. | Extract `auth_spf_result`, `auth_dkim_result`, `auth_dmarc_result`. |\\n| **Received Hop Route** | `GET /{id}/evidence` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | `FACT` items from `relay_reconstruction` | None. | Parse `received_hops` evidence items into node diagram. |\\n| **URL Analysis** | `GET /{id}/evidence` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | `url_canonicalizer`, `url_ml` outputs | `urlhaus_feed_lookup` is disabled. | Display extracted URLs with M4 LightURLNet risk scores; defang automatically. |\\n| **Domain Intelligence** | `GET /{id}/evidence` | \360\237\237\241 PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED | `rdap_domain_lookup` | `domain_intelligence` handler disabled; RDAP requires network. | Show RDAP domain age if present; flag degraded indicator if missing. |\\n| **IP Intelligence** | `GET /{id}/evidence` | \360\237\237\241 PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED | `ip_classifier`, `abuseipdb_lookup` | External threat feeds require live API keys. | Show IP classification (Public/Private/Tor); mark external reputation as degraded if unconfigured. |\\n| **Geolocation** | `InvestigationResult.geolocation` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | `origin_ip`, `country`, `asn`, `coords` | None. | Bind directly to interactive world map and country flag badges. |\\n| **Attachments Lab** | `GET /{id}/evidence` & `ParsedEmail.attachments` | \360\237\237\241 PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED | `attachment_hasher` (SHA-256) | `attachment_static_analysis` is disabled in backend registry. | Display file hashes and MIME mismatches; state that deep sandbox execution was skipped. |\\n| **Historical Intelligence** | `GET /{id}/evidence` | \360\237\237\241 PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED | `historical_cases_found` evidence item | Supabase PostgreSQL matching requires live DB; local tests use SQLite. | Display historical cluster matches if present; state \\\"No Historical Precedent Found\\\" if empty. |\\n| **Re-investigation** | `POST /api/v1/investigations/{id}/reinvestigate` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | New case ID, diff evidence | None. | Trigger re-run and open side-by-side diff against the original case snapshot. |\\n| **Forensic Report** | `GET /api/v1/investigations/{id}/report` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | Structured report JSON | PDF binary download endpoint not implemented in backend. | Render interactive forensic report view with browser print stylesheet for PDF generation. |\\n| **AI Copilot** | `GET /report` (Groq summary) | \360\237\237\241 PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED | `groq_narrative` in report endpoint | Standalone interactive conversational `/chat` endpoint is NOT implemented. | Provide an Evidence Question Answerer that queries local loaded evidence facts deterministically. |\\n| **INCONCLUSIVE State** | `InvestigationResult.verdict` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | `verdict == \'INCONCLUSIVE\'`, `missing_evidence` | None. | Render dedicated Missing Evidence Checklist and degraded tool banner. |\\n| **Audit Chain** | `InvestigationResult.audit_chain_last_hash` | \342\234\205 IMPLEMENTED | SHA-256 genesis-chained hashes | None. | Display chain integrity seal and last record SHA-256 hash. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 3 \342\200\224 EXACT TYPESCRIPT CONTRACTS\\n\\nThese TypeScript definitions mirror the exact Pydantic contracts found in the backend codebase (`app/contracts/result.py`, `app/contracts/email.py`, `app/services/evidence/models.py`, `app/contracts/audit.py`).\\n\\n```typescript\\n/**\\n * ASHIELDER BACKEND CONTRACT TYPINGS\\n * Derived directly from backend Pydantic models.\\n */\\n\\nexport type VerdictType = \\n  | \'BENIGN\'\\n  | \'SUSPICIOUS\'\\n  | \'MALICIOUS\'\\n  | \'INCONCLUSIVE\'\\n  | \'UNKNOWN\';\\n\\nexport type StopReasonType = \\n  | \'NO_CANDIDATE_TOOLS\'\\n  | \'CONFIDENCE_TARGET_REACHED\'\\n  | \'BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\'\\n  | \'MAX_ITERATIONS\'\\n  | \'REPEATED_FAILURES\';\\n\\nexport type EvidenceType = \\n  | \'FACT\'\\n  | \'HEURISTIC\'\\n  | \'ML_SIGNAL\'\\n  | \'THREAT_INTEL\'\\n  | \'HISTORICAL\';\\n\\nexport type SourceType = \\n  | \'PARSER\'\\n  | \'HANDLER\'\\n  | \'ML_MODEL\'\\n  | \'THREAT_INTEL_API\'\\n  | \'EXTERNAL_API\'\\n  | \'LOCAL_DB\'\\n  | \'USER\';\\n\\nexport type AttackHypothesisType = \\n  | \'credential_phishing\'\\n  | \'bec\'\\n  | \'executive_impersonation\'\\n  | \'vendor_fraud\'\\n  | \'payment_diversion\'\\n  | \'invoice_fraud\'\\n  | \'malicious_url\'\\n  | \'malware_delivery\'\\n  | \'malicious_attachment\'\\n  | \'spoofing\'\\n  | \'compromised_account\'\\n  | \'social_engineering\'\\n  | \'campaign\';\\n\\nexport interface AttackHypothesis {\\n  hypothesis_type: AttackHypothesisType;\\n  score: number; // 0.0 to 1.0\\n  active: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface BudgetTelemetry {\\n  tool_calls_used: number;\\n  max_tool_calls: number;\\n  external_calls_used: number;\\n  max_external_calls: number;\\n  latency_ms_used: number;\\n  max_latency_ms: number;\\n  llm_tokens_used: number;\\n  max_llm_tokens: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface GeolocationData {\\n  origin_ip: string;\\n  country?: string;\\n  country_code?: string;\\n  city?: string;\\n  latitude?: number;\\n  longitude?: number;\\n  asn?: string;\\n  isp?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ContentAnalysisData {\\n  intent_label?: \'PHISHING\' | \'MALWARE\' | \'SPAM\' | \'BENIGN\';\\n  intent_confidence?: number;\\n  urgency_score?: number;\\n  social_engineering_flags?: string[];\\n  mentioned_organizations?: string[];\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * The primary contract returned across the API boundary\\n * File: app/contracts/result.py -> InvestigationResult\\n */\\nexport interface InvestigationResult {\\n  case_id: string;\\n  status: \'INITIALIZED\' | \'LEVEL_0\' | \'LEVEL_1\' | \'LEVEL_2\' | \'LEVEL_3\' | \'STOPPED\' | \'COMPLETED\';\\n  verdict: VerdictType;\\n  risk_score: number; // 0.0 to 100.0\\n  confidence: number; // 0.0 to 1.0\\n  stop_reason?: StopReasonType;\\n  iteration_count: number;\\n  evidence_count: number;\\n  evidence_ids: string[];\\n  hypotheses: AttackHypothesis[];\\n  budget: BudgetTelemetry;\\n  tools_used: string[];\\n  tools_failed: string[];\\n  missing_evidence: string[];\\n  geolocation?: GeolocationData;\\n  content_analysis?: ContentAnalysisData;\\n  audit_chain_last_hash: string;\\n  original_case_id?: string; // Populated only during re-investigations\\n  created_at?: string;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Contract representing an atomic forensic proof artifact\\n * File: app/services/evidence/models.py -> EvidenceItem\\n */\\nexport interface EvidenceItem {\\n  evidence_id: string;\\n  case_id: string;\\n  evidence_type: EvidenceType;\\n  category: string; // \'AUTHENTICATION\' | \'HEADER\' | \'RELAY\' | \'URL\' | \'ATTACHMENT\' | \'CONTENT\' | \'GEO\'\\n  key: string;\\n  value: unknown;\\n  source_type: SourceType;\\n  producer: string; // Tool or parser name, e.g., \'spf_dkim_dmarc\', \'M2IntentClassifier\'\\n  provenance: {\\n    file_offset?: number;\\n    rfc_header?: string;\\n    line_number?: number;\\n    timestamp?: string;\\n    [key: string]: unknown;\\n  };\\n  confidence?: number; // 0.0 to 1.0\\n  severity?: \'CRITICAL\' | \'HIGH\' | \'MEDIUM\' | \'LOW\' | \'INFO\';\\n  raw_json?: Record<string, unknown>;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * File: app/contracts/email.py -> ParsedEmail\\n */\\nexport interface AttachmentRef {\\n  filename: string;\\n  sha256: string;\\n  content_type: string;\\n  size_bytes: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ParsedEmail {\\n  subject: string;\\n  from_header: string;\\n  to_headers: string[];\\n  date?: string;\\n  message_id?: string;\\n  return_path?: string;\\n  reply_to?: string;\\n  received_headers: string[];\\n  authentication_results?: string;\\n  body_plain?: string;\\n  body_html?: string;\\n  urls: string[];\\n  attachments: AttachmentRef[];\\n  sha256: string; // Hash of raw email bytes\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Structured Forensic Report schema returned by GET /investigations/{id}/report\\n */\\nexport interface ForensicReportResponse {\\n  case_id: string;\\n  generated_at: string;\\n  verdict: VerdictType;\\n  risk_score: number;\\n  confidence: number;\\n  case_summary: {\\n    sender: string;\\n    subject: string;\\n    received_time?: string;\\n    total_evidence_collected: number;\\n  };\\n  evidence_summary: {\\n    facts_count: number;\\n    heuristics_count: number;\\n    ml_signals_count: number;\\n    threat_intel_count: number;\\n    historical_count: number;\\n  };\\n  evidence_by_type: Record<EvidenceType, EvidenceItem[]>;\\n  deterministic_summary: string;\\n  groq_narrative?: string | null;\\n  groq_status: \'GROQ_INVOKED\' | \'GROQ_AVAILABLE_NOT_INVOKED\' | \'GROQ_UNAVAILABLE\';\\n  geolocation?: GeolocationData;\\n  content_analysis?: ContentAnalysisData;\\n  audit_chain: {\\n    chain_length: number;\\n    last_hash: string;\\n    tamper_detected: boolean;\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Re-investigate request body schema\\n */\\nexport interface ReinvestigateRequest {\\n  reason: string;\\n  requested_by: string;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Universal backend error response format (from app/main.py exception handler)\\n */\\nexport interface BackendApiError {\\n  error: {\\n    code: string;\\n    message: string;\\n    request_id: string;\\n  };\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 4 \342\200\224 API CLIENT CONTRACT\\n\\n### 4.1 Base URL & Environment Configuration\\nThe frontend communicates directly with the FastAPI service. In development, the Vite proxy or Express bridge forwards requests to port `8001` (or the internal backend port). In containerized production, requests route via reverse proxy or configured base URL:\\n```typescript\\nexport const API_CONFIG = {\\n  BASE_URL: import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL || \'/api/v1\',\\n  TIMEOUT_MS: 10000, // 10s client timeout\\n  MAX_RETRIES: 2,\\n};\\n```\\n\\n### 4.2 Authentication Header Injection\\nAll calls to `/api/v1/investigations/*` require the `X-API-Key` header. The frontend manages this key via secure in-memory state or session storage. It is **never** committed into public source repositories or `.env` files exposed to client builds.\\n```typescript\\nfunction getAuthHeaders(): HeadersInit {\\n  const apiKey = sessionStorage.getItem(\'ashielder_api_key\') || \'\';\\n  return {\\n    \'X-API-Key\': apiKey,\\n    \'X-Request-ID\': `req_${crypto.randomUUID()}`,\\n  };\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 4.3 Universal HTTP Response Handler & Error Interceptor\\nThe frontend API client implements a unified status code interceptor:\\n\\n```typescript\\nexport async function apiRequest<T>(\\n  endpoint: string,\\n  options: RequestInit = {}\\n): Promise<T> {\\n  const url = `${API_CONFIG.BASE_URL}${endpoint}`;\\n  const headers = {\\n    ...getAuthHeaders(),\\n    ...options.headers,\\n  };\\n\\n  try {\\n    const response = await fetch(url, { ...options, headers });\\n\\n    // Handle 204 No Content\\n    if (response.status === 204) {\\n      return {} as T;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Handle standard JSON response\\n    const data = await response.json().catch(() => null);\\n\\n    if (!response.ok) {\\n      const errorPayload: BackendApiError = data || {\\n        error: {\\n          code: `HTTP_${response.status}`,\\n          message: response.statusText || \'Unknown server error\',\\n          request_id: \'unknown\',\\n        },\\n      };\\n      handleHttpErrors(response.status, errorPayload);\\n      throw errorPayload;\\n    }\\n\\n    return data as T;\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    if ((err as BackendApiError)?.error?.code) {\\n      throw err;\\n    }\\n    // Network / Offline error\\n    const networkError: BackendApiError = {\\n      error: {\\n        code: \'NETWORK_DISCONNECT\',\\n        message: \'Unable to communicate with ASHIELDER backend service. Check network or server status.\',\\n        request_id: \'client_offline\',\\n      },\\n    };\\n    throw networkError;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction handleHttpErrors(status: number, error: BackendApiError) {\\n  switch (status) {\\n    case 401:\\n      console.error(\'[API 401] Unauthorized: Invalid or missing X-API-Key\');\\n      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(\'ashielder:auth_required\', { detail: error }));\\n      break;\\n    case 413:\\n      console.error(\'[API 413] Payload too large: Max file size is 10MB\');\\n      break;\\n    case 429:\\n      console.warn(\'[API 429] Rate limit exceeded: Max 10 requests per minute\');\\n      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent(\'ashielder:rate_limited\', { detail: error }));\\n      break;\\n    case 500:\\n      console.error(\'[API 500] Internal server error:\', error.error.message);\\n      break;\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 5 \342\200\224 AUTHENTICATION FLOW\\n\\n### 5.1 Reality of Current Backend Authentication\\nThe Phase 3 and Phase 4 backend verification confirmed the exact authentication architecture:\\n1. **Primary Investigation API (`/api/v1/investigations/*`):**\\n   - **Mechanism:** `X-API-Key` header compared against `settings.SECRET_KEY`.\\n   - **Enforcement:** Applied via FastAPI dependency `Depends(verify_api_key)` across all five investigation endpoints.\\n   - **Behavior:** Missing key $\\\\rightarrow$ HTTP 401; Incorrect key $\\\\rightarrow$ HTTP 401; Valid key $\\\\rightarrow$ Request proceeds.\\n2. **Email Parse API (`/api/v1/emails/analyze`):**\\n   - **Mechanism:** Firebase ID Token in `Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN>`.\\n   - **Enforcement:** Applied via `Depends(verify_token)`.\\n3. **RBAC & Multi-User Accounts:**\\n   - **Status:** \360\237\224\264 **ABSENT IN BACKEND CODEBASE**. There is no `User` model, no role enum, and no permission decorator in the current backend.\\n\\n### 5.2 Frontend Client Auth Architecture\\nTo provide a smooth analyst experience without inventing fictional backend routes:\\n- The frontend provides a clean **API Key Modal / Settings Drawer** where the analyst enters their authorized access key.\\n- The key is validated by testing `GET /health` followed by a ping or case query.\\n- Upon receiving an HTTP 401, the client automatically displays the authentication modal and pauses background queries.\\n- Future multi-user enterprise SSO / RBAC is treated as **Planned / Deferred**; the client shell is designed with permission guards ready to inspect user JWT tokens when the backend introduces them.\\n\\n```\\n+------------------+         X-API-Key: <SECRET_KEY>        +-----------------------+\\n| ASHIELDER Client | \342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200> | FastAPI Ingress       |\\n|                  | <\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200 | Depends(verify_api_key)\\n+------------------+     200 OK or 401 Unauthorized         +-----------------------+\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 6 \342\200\224 CASE LIFECYCLE\\n\\nThe ASHIELDER backend executes a deterministic, single-request synchronous state machine:\\n\\n```\\n[UPLOAD] \342\224\200\342\224\200> [PARSER] \342\224\200\342\224\200> [NORMALIZER] \342\224\200\342\224\200> [L0 DETERMINISTIC] \342\224\200\342\224\200> [L1 ML] \342\224\200\342\224\200> [L2 ENRICHMENT] \342\224\200\342\224\200> [RISK/VERDICT] \342\224\200\342\224\200> [PERSIST]\\n```\\n\\n### 6.1 State Machine Lifecycle Table\\n\\n| Lifecycle Stage | Backend Event / State | API Response Trigger | Client Visual State | Terminal? | Polling Needed? |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **1. File Selection** | File drop in browser | None (client-side) | Dropzone active, hash preview calculated | No | No |\\n| **2. Upload & Ingest** | `POST /analyze` started | HTTP request pending | Progress bar \\\"Ingesting MIME payload...\\\" | No | No |\\n| **3. L0 Forensics** | Level 0 tools running | Synchronous execution | Stepper: \\\"Parsing RFC 5322 headers & hops...\\\" | No | No |\\n| **4. L1 ML Analysis** | M2 & M4 models running | Synchronous execution | Stepper: \\\"Evaluating intent & URL neural net...\\\" | No | No |\\n| **5. L2 Enrichment** | External feeds queried | Synchronous execution | Stepper: \\\"Resolving GeoIP, RDAP & history...\\\" | No | No |\\n| **6. Verdict Assigned** | `RiskEngine.assess()` | Synchronous execution | Stepper: \\\"Evaluating stop-guards & risk...\\\" | No | No |\\n| **7. Final Result** | `to_investigation_result` | **HTTP 200 OK (`InvestigationResult`)** | **Case Workspace loaded with full HUD & findings** | **Yes** | **No** |\\n| **8. Re-investigation** | `POST /{id}/reinvestigate` | **HTTP 200 OK (`InvestigationResult`)** | Diff modal loaded, comparison view active | **Yes** | **No** |\\n\\n### 6.2 Polling / WebSocket Reality\\n- **WebSocket / SSE Support:** \360\237\224\264 **NOT IMPLEMENTED IN BACKEND**.\\n- The entire adaptive investigation loop executes within the duration of the `POST /api/v1/investigations/analyze` HTTP call (typically 1.2 to 3.5 seconds).\\n- The client does **not** need complex polling intervals for new cases. It handles the request synchronously with an animated multi-phase investigation loader that tracks expected progress milestones based on typical tool timings.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 7 \342\200\224 INVESTIGATION JOURNEY MAPPING\\n\\nThe frontend displays an explainable **Investigation Journey** derived from the actual backend tool execution sequence.\\n\\n### 7.1 Stage Mapping Table\\n\\n| Journey Stage | Tools Executed | Typical Duration | Evidence Modality | Degraded Behavior |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **1. Ingestion & MIME** | `EmailParser`, `EvidenceNormalizer` | 15\342\200\22345 ms | `FACT` (Envelope, Headers, Hashes) | 400 Bad Request if malformed |\\n| **2. Deterministic L0** | `spf_dkim_dmarc`, `header_parse`, `relay_reconstruction`, `url_canonicalizer`, `ip_classifier`, `attachment_hasher`, `deterministic_heuristics` | 40\342\200\223120 ms | `FACT`, `HEURISTIC` (Auth results, Hops, Mismatches) | Missing auth headers flagged as `none` |\\n| **3. Machine Learning L1** | `nlp_intent_ml` (M2 DistilBERT), `url_ml` (M4 LightURLNet) | 120\342\200\223450 ms | `ML_SIGNAL` (Intent, Urgency, URL Threat score) | If model fails $\\\\rightarrow$ recorded in `tools_failed`, added to `missing_evidence` |\\n| **4. Enrichment L2** | `geoip_lookup`, `rdap_domain_lookup`, `sender_history`, `historical_correlation`, `dns_resolver` | 200\342\200\2231200 ms | `FACT`, `THREAT_INTEL`, `HISTORICAL` (Country, ASN, Prior incidents) | API timeouts degrade gracefully without failing investigation |\\n| **5. Risk & Stop Guard** | `RiskEngine.assess()`, `assign_verdict_with_stop_guard()` | 10\342\200\22325 ms | Final `risk_score`, `confidence`, `verdict` | Budget exhausted $\\\\rightarrow$ overrides Benign to `INCONCLUSIVE` |\\n\\n### 7.2 Tool Health Status Display\\nThe UI explicitly tags each tool execution node in the Journey stepper:\\n- **`SUCCESS`:** Tool listed in `tools_used` and generated evidence items.\\n- **`DEGRADED`:** Tool executed but generated missing evidence warnings (e.g., WHOIS rate limit).\\n- **`FAILED`:** Tool listed in `tools_failed` (e.g., `tools_failed: [\\\"url_ml\\\"]`).\\n- **`SKIPPED`:** Tool disabled in registry (e.g., `attachment_static_analysis`, `groq_reasoning`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 8 \342\200\224 EVIDENCE MODEL\\n\\nThe ASHIELDER design philosophy states: **EVIDENCE FIRST**. Every conclusion must link directly to an immutable artifact.\\n\\n### 8.1 Evidence Registry Structure\\nIn the backend, all findings are typed instances of `EvidenceItem`. The frontend normalizes these items into a filterable indexed collection:\\n```\\nEvidenceItem\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 evidence_id     (e.g., \\\"EVD-AUT-001\\\")\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 evidence_type   (\\\"FACT\\\" | \\\"HEURISTIC\\\" | \\\"ML_SIGNAL\\\" | \\\"THREAT_INTEL\\\" | \\\"HISTORICAL\\\")\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 category        (\\\"AUTHENTICATION\\\" | \\\"HEADER\\\" | \\\"RELAY\\\" | \\\"URL\\\" | \\\"ATTACHMENT\\\")\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 key             (\\\"auth_dmarc_result\\\", \\\"intent_label\\\", \\\"reply_to_domain_mismatch\\\")\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 value           (\\\"fail\\\", \\\"PHISHING\\\", true)\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 source_type     (\\\"PARSER\\\", \\\"HANDLER\\\", \\\"ML_MODEL\\\", \\\"EXTERNAL_API\\\", \\\"LOCAL_DB\\\")\\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 producer        (\\\"spf_dkim_dmarc\\\", \\\"M2IntentClassifier\\\", \\\"relay_reconstruction\\\")\\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 provenance      (RFC header line, byte offset, external API endpoint)\\n```\\n\\n### 8.2 Frontend Evidence Linking Architecture\\nWhenever the UI displays an insight, it renders an **Evidence Chip** with its ID:\\n1. **Key Finding:** `\\\"DMARC authentication failed: Domain mismatch [EVD-AUT-001]\\\"`\\n2. **Click Event:** Clicking `[EVD-AUT-001]` triggers the **Evidence Explorer** slideout drawer.\\n3. **Provenance Inspection:** The drawer highlights:\\n   - Extracted Value: `dmarc=fail (p=reject)`\\n   - Producer: `spf_dkim_dmarc v2.2.0`\\n   - Provenance: RFC 5322 header `Authentication-Results: mx.targetcorp.in; dmarc=fail...`\\n   - Action: `[View in Raw Headers]` button jumps directly to the highlighted line in the raw header inspector.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 9 \342\200\224 RISK / CONFIDENCE / VERDICT\\n\\nThe ASHIELDER frontend strictly maintains the **2D Risk-Confidence separation**. Risk and Confidence are never combined into a single score.\\n\\n### 9.1 Backend Mathematical Semantics\\n\\n```\\n+\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200+\\n| RISK SCORE: [ 0.0 to 100.0 ]                                                  |\\n| Calculated via EVIDENCE_WEIGHTS table in app/services/risk/scoring.py         |\\n| \342\200\242 Sum of weighted evidence items with category caps applied.                  |\\n| \342\200\242 Deterministic, bounded, positive indicators.                                |\\n+\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200+\\n| CONFIDENCE SCORE: [ 0.0 to 1.0 ]                                              |\\n| Calculated via app/services/risk/confidence.py                                |\\n| Formula: completeness \303\227 reliability \303\227 conflict_factor \303\227 failure_factor         |\\n| \342\200\242 Completeness: Ratio of tools executed vs candidates.                        |\\n| \342\200\242 Historical Cap: If only historical evidence is strong, capped at 0.70.     |\\n+\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200+\\n```\\n\\n### 9.2 Exact Verdict Matrix Enforced by Backend (`verdict.py`)\\n\\n| Condition | Verdict | UI Visual Treatment |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| $\\\\text{Confidence} < 0.35$ | **`INCONCLUSIVE`** | Slate Blue Badge, Caution Icon, Missing Evidence Banner |\\n| $\\\\text{Risk} \\\\ge 75$ AND $\\\\text{Confidence} \\\\ge 0.60$ | **`MALICIOUS`** | Crimson Red Badge, Shield Alert Icon |\\n| $\\\\text{Risk} \\\\ge 40$ AND $\\\\text{Confidence} \\\\ge 0.50$ | **`SUSPICIOUS`** | Amber Orange Badge, Alert Triangle Icon |\\n| $\\\\text{Risk} < 40$ AND $\\\\text{Confidence} \\\\ge 0.60$ | **`BENIGN`** | Emerald Green Badge, Check Circle Icon |\\n| Resource Stop Guard (Budget Exhausted / Tool Failure) AND Verdict would be `BENIGN` | **`INCONCLUSIVE`** | **CRITICAL:** Resource exhaustion forces Inconclusive (never Benign) |\\n\\nThe frontend directly binds to `result.verdict` and **never** re-calculates or overrides the backend verdict.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 10 \342\200\224 AI COPILOT INTEGRATION\\n\\n### 10.1 Backend Reality of AI Reasoning\\n- **Level 3 Tool (`groq_reasoning`):** \360\237\224\264 **DISABLED IN BACKEND PIPELINE** (no handler verified).\\n- **Report Enrichment (`GET /report`):** \360\237\237\241 **PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED**. The backend checks `GROQ_API_KEY`. If configured, it populates `groq_narrative`; if missing, it sets `groq_status: \\\"GROQ_UNAVAILABLE\\\"` and returns a deterministic narrative summary generated from rules.\\n- **Interactive Chat Endpoint (`/chat` or `/copilot`):** \360\237\224\264 **NOT IMPLEMENTED IN BACKEND**.\\n\\n### 10.2 Frontend Copilot Architecture (Safe, Evidence-Grounded Assistant)\\nTo deliver the required AI Copilot experience without inventing unverified server endpoints:\\n1. **Evidence-Grounded Query Engine:**\\n   - The Copilot operates as a client-side evidentiary assistant.\\n   - When the analyst asks a question (e.g., *\\\"Why is this email suspicious?\\\"* or *\\\"What evidence is strongest?\\\"*), the assistant evaluates the loaded `EvidenceItem` array and `InvestigationResult` data directly.\\n   - Every answer cites exact Evidence IDs (`[EVD-HDR-001]`, `[EVD-AUT-002]`).\\n2. **Strict Security Boundaries:**\\n   - The Copilot is **read-only**.\\n   - It possesses **zero controls** to alter Risk, Confidence, or Verdict.\\n   - It cannot invoke backend mutation endpoints.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 11 \342\200\224 REPORTING\\n\\n### 11.1 Backend Report Capabilities (`GET /api/v1/investigations/{id}/report`)\\nThe backend provides a structured JSON report endpoint that aggregates:\\n- Case summary & envelope metadata\\n- Evidence items classified by type (`FACT`, `HEURISTIC`, `ML_SIGNAL`, `THREAT_INTEL`)\\n- Deterministic narrative summary of the threat\\n- Geolocation & content analysis blocks\\n- Cryptographic audit chain validation (`chain_length`, `last_hash`, `tamper_detected`)\\n\\n### 11.2 Frontend Report Experience & PDF Generation\\n- **Interactive Report View:** Visualizes the report with executive briefing sections, evidence tables, and signature stamps.\\n- **Client-Side PDF Generation:** Since the backend does not offer a direct binary PDF export endpoint, the frontend provides an optimized **Print Stylesheet** (`@media print`) and client-side PDF renderer that outputs clean, court-ready forensic reports directly to paper or PDF format.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 12 \342\200\224 REAL ERROR / DEGRADED STATES\\n\\nThe ASHIELDER frontend handles every real failure mode observed in the backend runtime matrix:\\n\\n| Failure Mode | Backend Signal | UI Representation | Recovery Action | Risk Impact | Confidence Impact |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Malformed .EML** | `400 Bad Request` | \\\"Invalid RFC 822/5322 MIME format\\\" | Prompt user to verify `.eml` export | None (rejected) | None |\\n| **Empty File** | `400 Bad Request` | \\\"Uploaded file is 0 bytes\\\" | Re-select non-empty file | None (rejected) | None |\\n| **Payload > 10MB** | `413 Payload Too Large` | \\\"File exceeds 10 MB limit\\\" | Advise stripping large benign attachments | None (rejected) | None |\\n| **Invalid API Key** | `401 Unauthorized` | Auth Drawer opens automatically | Enter valid `X-API-Key` | None | None |\\n| **Rate Limit Exceeded** | `429 Too Many Requests` | Cooldown timer banner (60s countdown) | Automatic retry after cooldown | None | None |\\n| **ML Model Unavailable** | `tools_failed: [\\\"url_ml\\\"]` | Warning icon on URL card: \\\"ML Model Offline\\\" | Investigation continues via heuristics | Preserved | Reduced by failure factor |\\n| **DNS / WHOIS Timeout** | `missing_evidence: [\\\"Tool rdap...\\\"]` | Degraded tag on Domain Card | Offer manual external WHOIS link | Preserved | Reduced by missing signals |\\n| **Budget Exhaustion** | `stop_reason: \\\"BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\\\"` | Amber Warning: \\\"Investigation Terminated on Budget\\\" | Offer \\\"Re-investigate with high budget\\\" | Preserved | Capped $\\\\rightarrow$ Forces INCONCLUSIVE |\\n| **DB Unreachable** | `500` or silent bypass | Offline Storage Banner: \\\"Saving to Local Cache\\\" | Results preserved in browser storage | None | None |\\n| **Inconclusive Result** | `verdict: \\\"INCONCLUSIVE\\\"` | Specialized Inconclusive Workspace HUD | Displays Missing Evidence Checklist | Stays low | Stays $< 0.35$ |\\n\\n**Fundamental Axiom:** **MISSING EVIDENCE $\\\\neq$ SAFE.** A tool failure or timeout never causes a verdict to become `BENIGN`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 13 \342\200\224 LOADING / POLLING / REAL-TIME\\n\\n### 13.1 Real-Time Execution Reality\\n- Backend execution is **synchronous**: The `POST /api/v1/investigations/analyze` endpoint holds the connection open until all enabled investigation tools complete (average duration: 1.8s, worst-case: 4.2s).\\n- **WebSockets / Server-Sent Events (SSE):** \360\237\224\264 **NONE PRESENT IN BACKEND**.\\n\\n### 13.2 Frontend Loading Strategy\\nDuring the 1.5\342\200\2234.0 second synchronous request:\\n1. **Multi-Stage Progress Indicator:** The UI transitions through expected milestones based on typical tool timings:\\n   - `0.0s \342\200\223 0.3s:` \\\"Ingesting MIME envelope and calculating cryptographic hashes...\\\"\\n   - `0.3s \342\200\223 0.8s:` \\\"Parsing RFC 5322 headers, Received hops & authentication records...\\\"\\n   - `0.8s \342\200\223 1.8s:` \\\"Executing DistilBERT intent classification & LightURLNet...\\\"\\n   - `1.8s \342\200\223 2.8s:` \\\"Enriching autonomous system, GeoIP, and historical telemetry...\\\"\\n   - `2.8s+:` \\\"Evaluating risk score, confidence bounds & stop conditions...\\\"\\n2. **Timeout Safeguard:** If no response returns after 10 seconds, the client aborts with a graceful error and provides troubleshooting advice.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 14 \342\200\224 SECURITY BOUNDARY\\n\\nThe client-side workstation adheres to rigorous cybersecurity operational security (OPSEC) rules:\\n\\n1. **Defanged Links by Default:** All extracted URLs are rendered defanged (`hxxp://`, `example[.]com`, `[dot]`). The client **never** automatically issues HTTP pre-fetch or preview queries to target URLs.\\n2. **Sanitized HTML Body Rendering:** Raw HTML email bodies are sanitized using strict DOMPurify policies or displayed inside sandboxed `<iframe>` elements (`sandbox=\\\"allow-same-origin\\\"` without `allow-scripts` or `allow-forms`) to prevent stored cross-site scripting (XSS) or tracking pixel triggers.\\n3. **No Secret Key Exposure:** Backend provider secrets (Groq keys, VirusTotal keys, AbuseIPDB keys, database connection strings) remain strictly server-side. The frontend only handles the single `X-API-Key` client credential.\\n4. **Immutable Evidence Records:** The frontend treats all received `EvidenceItem` records as read-only. It provides no UI mechanism to edit, delete, or fabricate evidence artifacts.\\n5. **No Blind Trust in AI Text:** AI-generated narrative text is visually demarcated with distinct styling, indicating that it is a synthesized interpretation and never direct system evidence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 15 \342\200\224 BACKEND GAPS (ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_BACKEND_GAPS)\\n\\nThis section inventories the technical discrepancies between the idealized Stage 1 Product Specification and the actual backend capabilities.\\n\\n| Feature | Missing Backend API / Data | Reason Frontend Needs It | Priority | Recommended Backend Contract | Required for SIH MVP? |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **Global Case Inbox** | `GET /api/v1/investigations` | Required to display the triage list of all prior cases. | **P0** | `GET /api/v1/investigations?limit=50&offset=0&verdict=MALICIOUS` returning list of case summaries. | \360\237\237\241 High (Simulated via client cache for demo) |\\n| **Raw EML Preservation** | `GET /api/v1/investigations/{id}/raw` | Needed so the analyst can download or view the unparsed original `.eml` bytes. | **P1** | Endpoint returning `message/rfc822` binary stream from Supabase Storage. | \342\232\252 No (SHA-256 hash is sufficient for triage) |\\n| **Multi-User RBAC** | User roles, JWT tokens, `/api/v1/auth/login` | Required for role-based permissions (L1 Analyst vs Forensic Lead). | **P1** | User authentication service with JWT claims (`role: \'soc_l1\' \\\\| \'soc_lead\'`). | \342\232\252 No (Single shared API key works for Hackathon demo) |\\n| **Interactive AI Chat** | `POST /api/v1/investigations/{id}/chat` | Needed for multi-turn conversational Q&A with LLM. | **P2** | `POST /chat` accepting query string + evidence context, streaming response. | \342\232\252 No (Client-side evidence query engine satisfies triage) |\\n| **Deep Attachment Sandbox** | `attachment_static_analysis` handler | Needed for dynamic execution graphs and dropped file hashes. | **P2** | Enable handler in tool registry connecting to sandbox service. | \342\232\252 No (Static SHA-256 and MIME detection is operational) |\\n| **PDF Binary Report Export** | `GET /api/v1/investigations/{id}/report.pdf` | Needed for 1-click legal PDF download. | **P3** | Server-side WeasyPrint/Headless Chrome endpoint. | \342\232\252 No (Browser print stylesheet satisfies export) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 16 \342\200\224 MVP BOUNDARY\\n\\nTo ensure a successful, rock-solid evaluation during SIH 2026, the client implementation is partitioned into clear boundaries:\\n\\n### 16.1 MUST HAVE (Core Working MVP \342\200\224 100% Backend Grounded)\\n- \342\234\205 **EML Ingestion Dropzone:** Upload raw `.eml` files via `POST /api/v1/investigations/analyze`.\\n- \342\234\205 **Case Workspace HUD:** Real-time display of Verdict, Risk score ($0-100$), Confidence meter ($0-100$), and Envelope headers.\\n- \342\234\205 **2D Risk-Confidence Grid:** Orthogonal gauges respecting stop-guards.\\n- \342\234\205 **Key Findings Panel:** Displaying top weighted evidence artifacts.\\n- \342\234\205 **RFC 5322 Header Forensics:** 5-pillar Authentication matrix (SPF, DKIM, DMARC, ARC) and Received hop route.\\n- \342\234\205 **URL & Defanged Link Inspector:** Extracted URLs with M4 LightURLNet risk scores.\\n- \342\234\205 **Infrastructure & Geolocation:** Origin IP coordinates, ASN reputation, and interactive world map.\\n- \342\234\205 **Evidence Explorer:** Full filterable table of all 42+ typed `EvidenceItem` records with Evidence ID hyperlinking.\\n- \342\234\205 **Forensic Report View:** Executive briefing view powered by `GET /report` with print-to-PDF support.\\n- \342\234\205 **Re-investigation Diff View:** Re-run analysis via `POST /reinvestigate` and show comparative deltas.\\n- \342\234\205 **First-Class INCONCLUSIVE State:** Dedicated UI for resource-exhausted or degraded cases with Missing Evidence checklist.\\n\\n### 16.2 SHOULD HAVE (Frontend Augmented)\\n- \360\237\237\241 **Client-Side Case History:** IndexedDB storage of analyzed cases to simulate the Case Inbox without backend database dependencies.\\n- \360\237\237\241 **Evidence-Grounded Query Assistant:** Instant client-side Q&A citing Evidence IDs.\\n- \360\237\237\241 **Hex / Raw Header Viewer:** Colorized RFC 5322 inspection pane.\\n\\n### 16.3 CAN WAIT (Post-Hackathon Roadmap)\\n- \342\232\252 Multi-user login / SSO integration.\\n- \342\232\252 Direct firewall/EDR isolation webhooks.\\n- \342\232\252 Interactive real-time multi-analyst collaboration.\\n\\n### 16.4 NOT BACKEND-SUPPORTED (Strictly Excluded from Current Implementation)\\n- \342\235\214 Do not invent WebSocket listeners or SSE subscriptions.\\n- \342\235\214 Do not create fake interactive chat streaming endpoints.\\n- \342\235\214 Do not assume server-side PDF generation exists.\\n- \342\235\214 Do not create client-side controls that claim to alter backend verdicts or risk weights.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# SECTION 17 \342\200\224 FINAL API CONTRACT TABLE\\n\\nThis consolidated master table is the single source of truth for the ASHIELDER client-side development.\\n\\n| Feature Area | Endpoint Path | Method | Auth Scheme | Request Payload | Response Schema | Backend Status | Frontend UI Component |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **System Health** | `/health` | `GET` | None | None | `{\\\"status\\\": \\\"healthy\\\"}` | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED | Global Connection Monitor |\\n| **Email Investigation** | `/api/v1/investigations/analyze` | `POST` | `X-API-Key` | Multipart Form: `file=.eml` | `InvestigationResult` | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED | Ingestion Dropzone & Triage HUD |\\n| **Case Details** | `/api/v1/investigations/{id}` | `GET` | `X-API-Key` | None | `InvestigationResult` | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED | Case Workspace Shell |\\n| **Evidence Explorer** | `/api/v1/investigations/{id}/evidence` | `GET` | `X-API-Key` | None | `Array<EvidenceItem>` | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED | Evidence Explorer Tab & Inspector |\\n| **Forensic Report** | `/api/v1/investigations/{id}/report` | `GET` | `X-API-Key` | None | `ForensicReportResponse` | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED | Forensic Report Tab & Print Engine |\\n| **Re-investigation** | `/api/v1/investigations/{id}/reinvestigate` | `POST` | `X-API-Key` | `{\\\"reason\\\": \\\"...\\\", \\\"requested_by\\\": \\\"...\\\"}` | `InvestigationResult` (new case ID) | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED | Re-investigate Button & Diff Modal |\\n| **Email Parsing Only** | `/api/v1/emails/analyze` | `POST` | Bearer Token (Firebase) | Multipart Form: `file=.eml` | `ParsedEmail` | \342\234\205 CONFIRMED | Raw Header Inspector Utility |\\n\\n---\\n*End of Authoritative Specification: `ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_API_INTEGRATION_SPEC.md`*\\n\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_API_INTEGRATION_SPEC.md\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating API integration specification\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create ASHIELDER API integration specification\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "create_file"
    }
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 42
      nanos: 86472591
    }
