  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Research and define the complete ASHIELDER client experience:** (PHASE: COMPLETED)\n  - The user requested the creation of `ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md` and `ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_API_INTEGRATION_SPEC.md`. Both documents have been authored and finalized based on the provided backend E2E traces.\n- **Frontend Implementation:** (PHASE: NOT STARTED)\n  - The user has not yet requested the actual implementation (coding) of the frontend components. The current work has been focused exclusively on product and API specification.\n\n2. User Knowledge\n- **Role:** Senior Product Designer, UX Architect, Cybersecurity SOC UX Specialist, and Frontend Product Architect.\n- **Project:** ASHIELDER (AI-Powered Email Threat Detection, GeoLocation & Forensic Intelligence Platform, SIH 2026 PS 26106).\n- **Core Principles:** \"Evidence First,\" \"Summary Before Detail,\" \"Current Case \342\211\240 Historical Context,\" \"System Finding \342\211\240 AI Explanation,\" \"Risk \342\211\240 Confidence,\" \"Missing Evidence \342\211\240 Safe,\" \"AI is Assistant, not Authority.\"\n- **Constraints:**\n  - \"Do NOT design or invent backend functionality.\"\n  - \"Do NOT write code\" (during the specification phase).\n  - \"The UI must feel like: Professional SOC platform + Digital Forensics workstation + Modern enterprise dashboard + AI copilot.\"\n  - \"It must NOT look like: ChatGPT clone, generic SaaS dashboard, gaming UI, hacker/cyberpunk interface, overly futuristic interface.\"\n\n3. Work Accomplished\n- **Frontend Product Specification:** Created `ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md`, detailing the information architecture, navigation, case workspace, forensic report experience, and design system.\n- **Backend API Integration Specification:** Created `ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_API_INTEGRATION_SPEC.md`. This document maps the frontend requirements to the actual backend implementation (Phase 2-4 E2E traces), defining API contracts, TypeScript interfaces, authentication flows, and backend gaps.\n- **Backend Verification:** Analyzed provided backend E2E traces to ensure the frontend specification is grounded in real-world backend capabilities (e.g., synchronous investigation pipeline, evidence types, risk/confidence scoring, and error handling).\n\n4. Model Knowledge\n- **Backend Architecture:** The ASHIELDER backend is a deterministic, synchronous investigation engine built with FastAPI. It uses a multi-level adaptive investigation loop (L0 deterministic, L1 ML, L2 enrichment).\n- **Authentication:** Authenticated via `X-API-Key` header for investigation endpoints. Firebase token for email parsing. RBAC/SSO is currently absent.\n- **Evidence Model:** Evidence is the central data model. Every finding is an `EvidenceItem` with a specific type (FACT, HEURISTIC, ML_SIGNAL, THREAT_INTEL, HISTORICAL) and provenance.\n- **Risk/Confidence:** These are orthogonal metrics. They must never be merged.\n- **Verdict Logic:** The backend enforces a \"Resource-Stop Guard.\" If the investigation budget is exhausted or a tool fails, the verdict is forced to `INCONCLUSIVE` (never `BENIGN`).\n- **AI Copilot:** The reasoning layer (Groq) is advisory and grounded in evidence. It cannot modify verdicts, risk, or confidence.\n\n5. Files and Code\n- **Edited/Created Files:**\n  - `/ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md`: Comprehensive frontend product specification.\n  - `/ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_API_INTEGRATION_SPEC.md`: API integration specification based on backend contracts.\n  - `/metadata.json`: Updated with project name and description.\n  - `/index.html`: Updated title and meta tags for the ASHIELDER platform.\n- **Viewed Files:**\n  - `/src/App.tsx`: Inspected to confirm application context.\n  - `/metadata.json`: Inspected for project metadata.\n  - `/index.html`: Inspected for SEO/meta configuration.\n\n6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Current Work:** The specification phase is complete. The user has successfully defined the product vision and the technical API contracts required for implementation.\n- **Next Steps:**\n  - The next agent should proceed to the **Implementation Phase** if requested by the user.\n  - The implementation should strictly follow the `ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_PRODUCT_SPEC.md` for UI/UX and `ASHIELDER_FRONTEND_API_INTEGRATION_SPEC.md` for API interactions.\n  - **Immediate priority:** Begin implementing the core Case Inbox and Case Workspace components, ensuring the 2D Risk-Confidence HUD and Evidence Explorer are bound to the verified API contracts."
    included_step_index_start: 1
